<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10945" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contūsĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		contundo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a crushing, breaking, battering, bruising</i>
			(rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">olivae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 47, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">falcis hebetioris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 24, 37, § 227</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			medic. language, <i>a bruise, contusion</i>, <i><span class="en">Scrib.
				Comp. 101</span></i>; <i><span class="en">165</span></i> et saep.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
